    "text": "By Julian Hayes ,\n2 hours ago The best time to paddle is just after sunrise, when the wind has not woken up yet and the water lies flat as glass. One Oklahoma reservoir turns into a kayaker’s paradise during those early hours, with herons gliding silently along the shoreline and the only sound coming from your paddle dipping into the surface. Read full article",
